# SKILL.md Entry Point Format

Follow [agentskills-best-practices.md](../docs/agentskills-best-practices.md) §4 and §8. Validate with `npm run validate`.

## Required frontmatter

```yaml
---
name: skill-name-here
description: Use this skill when...
metadata:
  version: "1.0.0"
---
```

### `name`

- Max 64 characters; lowercase letters, numbers, hyphens only
- Must match parent directory name
- No leading/trailing/consecutive hyphens

### `description`

- Max 1024 characters, non-empty
- **Imperative framing:** "Use this skill when…" — tell the agent when to act
- Include **what** the skill does, **when** to trigger, and **keywords** users might say
- Focus on user intent, not internal file layout
- Surface skills may err pushy on scope (include related contexts even without explicit keywords)
- Router skills own ambiguous triggers; surface skills own specific implementation keywords — avoid keyword competition in a skill family

### Optional fields

- `compatibility` — only when environment requirements exist (≤ 500 chars)
- `metadata.version` — include on all skills in this repo

## Body structure

- **Under 500 lines.** Split detailed content into `references/`.
- Brief heading + one-line summary near top
- **Quick start** or core routing early
- **Guardrails** (Never / Always) near top
- **Mandatory read order** when references are load-bearing — tell the agent *when* to load each file
- **Task progress** checklist for multi-step workflows
- Link references one level deep: `references/guide.md`, not chains of nested files

## Progressive disclosure

`SKILL.md` is a router, not an encyclopedia. Point to `references/` for depth. Example trigger:

> Read `references/tool-design.md` before authoring any paid tools.

## Online documentation

For SolvaPay APIs: online-first with local fallback in `references/`. For well-known third-party tools, linking to official docs without a fallback is acceptable.
